cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "G4-WATCH: a G-quadruplex genomic early-warning framework for livestock viruses"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ICAR-NIVEDI"
    address: "ICAR-National Institute of Veterinary Epidemiology and Disease Informatics"
    city: Bengaluru
    country: IN
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - g-quadruplex
  - genomic surveillance
  - veterinary virology
  - foot-and-mouth disease virus
  - phylogenetics
abstract: >-
  G4-WATCH is a reproducible pipeline for identifying and monitoring
  G-quadruplex-forming loci in livestock virus genomes. Surveillance
  scoring is contingent on a per-pathogen statistical gate (the D.H1
  test), which compares phylogenetically-weighted, GC-adjusted disruption
  at G4 loci against matched control regions. Scoring remains unwired
  until that gate returns SUPPORTED, so a negative or insufficient-data
  outcome is reported as a finding rather than filled in with
  unsupported numbers. As of this release the FMDV gate reports
  INSUFFICIENT_DATA owing to real per-serotype undersampling.
references:
  - type: software
    title: PhiPack
    notes: "Recombination screening (PHI test); GPL-3.0; invoked as a separate executable."
    repository-code: "https://github.com/julianzaugg/phipack"
